<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF wins Kazakh radar contract.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF wins Kazakh radar contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF said on Tuesday its Thomson-CSF Airsys subsidiary has won a 150 million franc contract to supply a radar-based air traffic control system to Kazakhstan's civil aviation authority.</p>
<p>The contract is for the first phase of the programme and involves supply and installation of three Star 2000 solid-state primary radars for approach control of the country's main airports, Thomson-CSF said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
